"Manaweaving How-To": {
  "index": 0,
  "category": "manaweaving",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "What is Manaweaving"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Manaweaving",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " is the process of infusing my own magic into my creations. Spells, rituals, runes, and more can make use of it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "To do it, I must first craft a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Manaweaver's Wand",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nThe "
        },
        {
          "text": "improvised and vinteum wands",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " have limited uses and "
        },
        {
          "text": "will eventually break",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", however I'm certain I can make more powerful ones that will "
        },
        {
          "text": "last forever if I can find the right materials to do so",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "location": "mna:vinteum_manaweaver_wand",
      "scale": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Once I have my wand crafted, I need to hold the wand in my hand and begin channeling magic through the wand (hold the right mouse button). Then, I carefully draw the shape in the air.  \n\nOnce I stop channeling magic, if I've done it right, the pattern will appear in the air in front of me."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "location": "mna:textures/guide/manaweaving.png",
      "width": 128,
      "height": 128
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "The concentration required will consume my mana quickly. "
        },
        {
          "text": "I should not rush",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", however, lest I make mistakes: "
        },
        {
          "text": "an incorrectly pattern will do nothing",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nSome mages claim to have heard "
        },
        {
          "text": "chimes while using",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " a manaweaver wand. While not confirmed, such an occurrence would be an "
        },
        {
          "text": "indication that the wand is working",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nThere are also those that are either "
        },
        {
          "text": "unable or unwilling to draw the shapes in the air",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nTo that end, the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Manaweave Projector",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " was developed. Simply place it on the ground and it will draw in my mana (or that of others nearby) to power itself. When activated, it will project the pattern it is set to after a few seconds.\n\nI can also "
        },
        {
          "text": "prepare manaweaves in advance",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " by "
        },
        {
          "text": "capturing a drawn manaweave",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " in a "
        },
        {
          "text": "simple glass bottle",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  It will remain there until I need it.  I can release the manaweave by throwing the bottle, which unfortunately breaks the glass but instantly recreates the manaweave at the point the bottle landed.  I'm sure I can automate bottling manaweaves too, if I'm clever."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "location": "mna:textures/guide/manaweave_projector.png",
      "width": 48,
      "height": 128
    }
  ],
